// Registry 221.1 #889 -- REPRO. `nova check` green, `nova build` fails in C
// (undeclared identifier 'Nova_Pair' / NovaTuple_Pair).
// NOTE the direction of the fix: D215 says construction of a paren-declared
// type is POSITIONAL (`Vec3(1.0, 2.0, 3.0)`, amendment 2026-08-05). The brace
// form is not a construction form the spec defines -- so the defect is that
// the CHECKER ACCEPTS it, not that codegen fails to support it.
module brace_on_paren_type

type Named(x int, y int)

fn main() Io -> () {
    ro p = Named { x: 1, y: 2 }
    println(p.x)
}
